    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32567" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnĭgĕnus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		omnis-genus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of all kinds</i> (<b>poet.</b> and
			in post-class. prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnigenūmque deūm monstra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 8, 698</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnigenūm genitor deūm,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 9, § 912</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">doctrinae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					14, 6, 1</span></i>
			 (but in <i><span class="en">Lucr. 2, 759</span></i>; <i><span class="en">821 al.</span></i> Lachm. reads
			omne genus).</div>
